        "original_id": "095d5145-5859-57fc-9f55-9cce048a8371",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Mikael Åkerfeldt, Lee Ranaldo, Thurston Moore, Steven Wilson, Lunch, Martin Bisi\n- Bands/Projects: Opeth, Bloodbath, Steel, Storm Corrosion, Sonic Youth\n- Songs: \"Death Valley '69\"\n- Publications/Lists: Rolling Stone, Spin\n\nFacts:\n- Mikael Åkerfeldt was born on 17 April 1974 and is a Swedish musician.\n- Lee Ranaldo was born on February 3, 1956 and is an American musician, singer-songwriter, guitarist, writer, visual artist, and record producer.\n- In 1984, Martin Bisi recorded the song \"Death Valley '69.\"\n- \"Death Valley '69\" was written and sung by Thurston Moore and the New York musician Lunch.\n- In 2004, Rolling Stone ranked Lee Ranaldo at number 33 on its \"Greatest Guitarists of All Time\" list.\n- In May 2012, Spin published a staff-selected top 100 ranking that placed Thurston Moore and his Sonic Youth bandmate Lee Ranaldo together at number 1.\n- Mikael Åkerfeldt is the lead vocalist, guitarist, and primary songwriter of Opeth.\n- Mikael Åkerfeldt is the former vocalist of Bloodbath.\n- Mikael Åkerfeldt was also guitarist for the one-off band Steel.\n- Mikael Åkerfeldt is part of Storm Corrosion with Steven Wilson.\n- Lee Ranaldo is best known as a co-founder of Sonic Youth.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
